>> title: Hill Chili
>> tags: chili, venison, beans
>> prep time:
>> cook time: 1 hour

This venison chili recipe is a hearty and flavorful dish that is perfect for a cold day. It is made with ground venison, vegetables, and a variety of spices for a delicious and satisfying meal.

Add @ground beef{1%lb} (venison) to a #pot{} with a little @oil{} and brown it.

Add @onion{1%medium}, chopped, @red bell pepper{1/2}, chopped, and @Soyrizo{1/2%package}. Saute until soft.

Add @crushed tomatoes{1%large can}, @Rotel{1%small can}, @kidney beans{2%15 oz cans}, rinsed, @chili beans{2%15 oz cans}, @Lipton Onion Soup mix{1%package}, @cumin{1/2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @chili powder{1%tbsp}, @cayenne pepper{1/4%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Simmer for ~simmer{1%hour}. Optionally pressure cook.

= Optional toppings

Serve with @sour cream{}, more @onion{}, and @cilantro{}.
